ognize this might be a skill issue) most things I found are either SEO slop or trying to sell/market some service.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor some more context and to give a concrete example as to what I'm interested in, I got my hands on a Raspberry Pi which I'd like to use to start tinkering with self-hosting. My main goal would be to host my (static) website on it, potentially adding more things in the future.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSome people I asked this question recommended solutions like Cloudflare Tunnels to make it secure, but using such a provider almost feels like it defeats the point of self-hosting, so I'm curious whether it's viable to do it using open source tooling, any gotchas one might encounter, and generally any thoughts you might have on the topic.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e(Also, feel free to suggest a tag other than \u003ccode\u003edevops\u003c/code\u003e, I figured \u003ccode\u003esecurity\u003c/code\u003e doesn't quite apply since it's a question and not a write-up/resource regarding security.)\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"I recognize that the title is rather vague, but I'm completely green when it comes to self-hosting, so I figured here would be a good place to ask for some pointers given the discussions I sometimes see happening in the comments. I tried researching first through DDG and Google, but (and I recognize this might be a skill issue) most things I found are either SEO slop or trying to sell/market some service.\r\n\r\nFor some more context and to give a concrete example as to what I'm interested in, I got my hands on a Raspberry Pi which I'd like to use to start tinkering with self-hosting. My main goal would be to host my (static) website on it, potentially adding more things in the future.\r\n\r\nSome people I asked this question recommended solutions like Cloudflare Tunnels to make it secure, but using such a provider almost feels like it defeats the point of self-hosting, so I'm curious whether it's viable to do it using open source tooling, any gotchas one might encounter, and generally any thoughts you might have on the topic.\r\n\r\n(Also, feel free to suggest a tag other than `devops`, I figured `security` doesn't quite apply since it's a question and not a write-up/resource regarding security.)","submitter_user":"pralkarz","user_is_author":true,"tags":["ask","devops"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/m43bas","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/m43bas/how_do_you_actually_self_host_securely"},{"short_id":"ubbxhd","created_at":"2026-11-12T08:37:35.465-06:00","title":"The Secret of Monkey Island: all 13 versions side by side","url":"https://monkeyisland.pages.dev/","score":13,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"HugoDaniel","user_is_author":false,"tags":["games","graphics"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ubbxhd","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ubbxhd/secret_monkey_island_all_13_versions_side"},{"short_id":"nld6x3","created_at":"2026-11-11T07:13:51.549-06:00","title":"What are some \"No AI\" apps/companies/resources you know of?","url":"","score":92,"flags":1,"comment_count":45,"description":"\u003cp\u003eHey everyone I'm wondering if there's any useful/helpful list of apps, companies, or resources in general that avoid AI (they don't have to be vocally or openly \"anti\", but at least explicitly avoid it) that you know of?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI'm not looking to start a discussion on what's good/bad or (un)worthy about AI, or who's for/against, just links and/or communities promoting this sentiment/position.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor example, \u003ca href=\"https://www.rebeltechalliance.org\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ehttps://www.rebeltechalliance.org\u003c/a\u003e would be one of those resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThank you!\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Hey everyone I'm wondering if there's any useful/helpful list of apps, companies, or resources in general that avoid AI (they do